    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled on one of Malahide's most sought-after residential roads, Hermanus is an exceptional double-fronted detached family residence enjoying an enviable village-centre setting. Located on prestigious Grove Road, this distinguished home is just a leisurely stroll from the picturesque coastline, vibrant marina and the heart of Malahide Village, where an abundance of renowned restaurants, boutiques, cafés, schools and recreational amenities await.\nOccupying magnificent, mature gardens extending to approximately 0.185 hectares (0.45 acres), amongst the largest private gardens in the village centre, Hermanus offers a rare combination of generous family accommodation, exceptional privacy and unrivalled convenience.\nMalahide itself is one of Dublin's most desirable coastal villages, celebrated for its charming atmosphere, excellent schools, tennis clubs, DART station and the historic Malahide Castle and Gardens. The scenic coastal walk to Portmarnock's Silver Strand Beach further enhances the area's appeal.\nBehind its elegant façade lies a wonderfully spacious and light-filled interior extending to beautifully proportioned accommodation designed for family living. A welcoming porch opens into an impressive reception hall featuring herringbone oak flooring, decorative coving and an attractive staircase to the first floor. An understairs shoe and storage nook adds both character and functionality.\nThe elegant L-shaped drawing room enjoys dual-aspect views over the front and rear gardens and centres around a charming wood-burning stove set upon a raised black marble hearth. Double doors connect seamlessly to the sunroom and garden beyond.\nPositioned off the opposite side of the hall, a comfortable family/TV room provides a cosy retreat and features a raised electric fireplace, a TV insert and dual-aspect windows. To the rear, the large formal dining room benefits from dual-aspect natural light, Junkers oak flooring and sliding patio doors opening to the conservatory overlooking the gardens.\nAt the heart of the home lies an outstanding open-plan L-shaped kitchen and breakfast area, perfectly designed for contemporary family life. The kitchen is fitted with a stylish German-designed high-gloss kitchen complemented by quality integrated appliances, a sloping painted ceiling with recessed lighting, Velux windows and tiled flooring throughout. This superb space flows effortlessly into a large sun-drenched conservatory with a modern wall mounted wood burning stove. A generously proportioned utility room with matching fitted cabinetry and side access is located just off the kitchen. \nThe rear conservatory corridor provides access to an excellent games room overlooking the front garden, while a spacious home office and guest WC complete the ground-floor accommodation.\nUpstairs, the accommodation continues to impress with six generously proportioned bedrooms. The principal suite features a walk-in dressing room and ensuite bathroom, while Bedrooms Two and Three share a Jack-and-Jill bathroom. A beautifully appointed fully tiled family bathroom includes a steam room with a large rain shower, heated towel rail and contemporary fittings.\nOutside\nApproached through electronic wrought-iron gates, Hermanus is set within exceptionally private and mature grounds extending to approximately 0.185 hectares. The front garden provides extensive secure off-street parking framed by established lawns, mature hedging and colourful planting.\nA wide side entrance leads to the remarkable rear garden, a true highlight of the property. Exceptionally large and wonderfully private, it features expansive patio areas, extensive lawns, mature trees, specimen planting and well-established boundaries. A bespoke pergola creates the perfect setting for outdoor entertaining, al fresco dining and summer barbecues.\nAdditional features include a boiler house, garden shed, steel-framed storage shed and a former putting green offering potential for reinstatement or alternative recreational use. Several secluded seating areas capture the sun throughout the day and into the evening, making the garden an exceptional outdoor sanctuary.\nRarely does a property of such distinction, scale and setting come to the market within the heart of Malahide Village. Combining elegant family accommodation, exceptional gardens and a highly coveted coastal location, Hermanus represents a truly unique opportunity.\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate all that this outstanding residence has to offer."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - 3.56m x 1.17m\nLarge entrance porch with tiled flooring, double glazed windows to front, storage cupboard\n\nStorage - 0.69m x 0.58m\nStorage cupboard located in porch\n\nEntrance Hall - 7.08m x 2.67m\nLarge Entrance hall with solid oak Herringbone flooring\n\nKitchen/ Breakfast Room - 10.10m x 3.31m\nOpen plan kitchen and breakfast room with conservatory to rear. High gloss German kitchen from Rational Küchen with quality integrated appliances such as Miele oven and microwave, De Dietrich gas hob and extractor fan, Miele Dishwasher, sink unit. Large central island with an abundance of storage. Overhead spotlights throughout and Velux skylights.\n\nConservatory - 4.25m x 3.00m\nBright conservatory to the rear with double glazed windows and sliding doors to garden. Further enhance by a raised solid fuel fireplace by Wanders, Velux skylights and spotlights. Tiled flooring throughout\n\nDining Room - 5.46m x 3.85m\nSpacious dining room with Yonkers wooden flooring, double glazed windows and double French doors to conservatory\n\nDrawing Room - 5.63m x 3.77m\n+ 3.32m x 2.92m, Formal drawing room with large bay window (4.23m x 1.09m), raised BG solid fuel fireplace, Yonkers wooden flooring, coving on ceiling with ornate centre piece and French doors to sunroom\n\nFamily Room - 4.80m x 3.33m\nComprising raised electric fireplace with Quartz finish, Yonkers flooring, coving with ornate centre piece, double glazed windows\n\nOffice - 3.40m x 2.91m\nYonkers wooden flooring, double glazed window to sunroom\n\nInner hall - 1.77m x 1.01m\nOak herringbone floor\n\nGuest Wc - 1.60m x 1.20m\nTiled guest wc comprising hand wash basin and low level wc\n\nSunroom/ Link - 4.86m x 2.18m\n+ 3.56m x 2.21m. Double glazed windows and French doors to rear patio, tiled flooring throughout, entrance to games room\n\nStore 1 - 1.40m x 1.40m\n\n\nStore 2 - 1.76m x 0.95m\n\n\nGames Room - 5.18m x 3.00m\nYonkers wooden flooring and double glazed window to front\n\nUtility Room - 3.53m x 2.11m\nBuilt in storage cupboards with extra sink unit, plumbing for washing machine and dryer, granite work tops, door to rear\n\nUPSTAIRS - \n\n\nLanding - 5.41m x 1.77m\nLarge carpet landing with solid wood balustrade, coving with ornate centre piece, access to partially floored attic via pull down Stira\n\nPrincipal Bedroom - 3.85m x 3.24m\n+3.44m x 1.67m. Large principal bedroom with double glazed window overlooking rear gardens, Yonkers oak flooring, dado railing, Velux skylight and built in wardrobe\n\nEnsuite - 2.20m x 1.51m\nFully tiled ensuite comprising shower, hand wash basin, wc and heated towel rail, frosted window to rear\n\nDressing Room - 2.10m x 1.51m\nAmple storage with hanging rails\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.24m x 3.16m\n+ 1.53m x 1.10m. Built in wardrobes, double glazed windows and oak Yonkers flooring, access to ensuite\n\nJack & Jill Bathroom - 2.00m x 1.80m\nFully tiled comprising shower, hand wash basin with storage, wc and frosted window\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.52m x 3.34m\n+ 1.54m x 0.98m. Built in wardrobes, double glazed windows and oak Yonkers flooring, access to ensuite\n\nFamily Bathroom - 3.44m x 1.70m\nLarge high gloss tiled bathroom comprising large walk in steam room with a rainfall shower, large hand wash basin with vanity, wc, bidet, frosted window\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.28m x 3.00m\nGuest room with storage cupboard, double glazed window to rear and oak Yonkers flooring\n\nBedroom 5 - 2.27m x 2.24\n+ 2.91m x 2.53m. Dressing area with built in cupboards, double glazed windows to rear and oak Yonkers flooring. Sleeping area with double glazed window and oak Yonkers flooring\n\nBedroom 6 - 3.80m x 2.40m\nOak Yonkers flooring throughout and double glazed window\n\n"
      },
